-- title:
--   Non-vanishing node residue forces a unit in the local node ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a level $N \neq 0$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$, together with a modular polynomial datum `data` for $q$ (a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb Z[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ annihilating the $q$-division $j$-series), a proof `hKr` that $\Phi$ reduces modulo $q$ to $(X^q - Y)(X - Y^q)$ in the stated bivariate form, integrality hypotheses $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ for the Hecke $\bar\alpha$- and $\bar\beta$-homomorphisms at level $N$ and prime $q$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a place specialization $P$ for these data, and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$. Assume $k$ is algebraically closed with decidable equality and $q \nmid N$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of the modular function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$ (the subfield of $k((q))$ generated by the reductions of $j$ and $j_N$), each lying in $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\ q\ N\ k$, i.e. supersingular, and suppose $R$ satisfies the regularity law on $W$: residues of integral elements are regular at Frobenius-fixed affine geometric places, and at node pairs of $W$ the two residues take a common value. Let $K \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ be an intermediate field finite-dimensional over $\mathbb Q$ and let $w \in W$. Assume the subring $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\ K\ w$ — those elements of the ring `R.nodeIntegers w` whose underlying Laurent series lies in $\mathrm{NodeLocalized.fieldOver}\ (N q)\ K$ — is a local ring, and let $s$ be one of its elements. If either the first node residue of $s$ fails to take the value $0$ at $w$, or the second node residue of $s$ fails to take the value $0$ at the place $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\ q\ k\ N \cdot w$ obtained by translating $w$ by the coefficientwise $q$-power Frobenius semilinear automorphism (where 'takes the value $a$ at $v$' means lying in the valuation subring of $v$ with residue the image of $a$), then $s$ is a unit of $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\ K\ w$.
--
--   This is the unit criterion for the local ring of the modular curve $X_0(Nq)$ at a supersingular node, in the form needed for the prolongation-tuple formalism: evaluation of the first node residue at $w$ cuts out exactly the maximal ideal. It is used in the identification of the maximal ideal of the node ring and in the saturation statements for node residues under the order law.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_PlaceSpecialization_ProlongationTuple_isUnit_of_not_hasValue_nodeResidue_zero_of_isLocalRing.lean

